 ('ENT_FINN_POHJOLA','PER_FINN_TRADITIONAL','The dark northern otherworld of the Kalevala, ruled by Louhi, where the Sampo was forged and hidden inside a copper mountain.'),
 ('ENT_BALT_PANTHEON','PER_BALT_PAGAN','Collective grouping of the deities and spirits of the Baltic peoples (Lithuanian, Latvian, Old Prussian) as reconstructed by Gimbutas and Greimas from folklore and medieval chronicles.'),
 ('ENT_BALT_AUSRINE','PER_BALT_PAGAN','The morning star personified, Lithuanian Aušrinė (a goddess, daughter of the sun Saulė) and Latvian Auseklis (a male morning-star figure of the daina songs).'),
 ('ENT_BALT_USINS','PER_BALT_PAGAN','Latvian god of horses, bees, and the returning light of spring, celebrated at the festival marking the start of pasturing.'),
 ('ENT_BALT_BANGPUTYS','PER_BALT_PAGAN','Lithuanian god of the sea and storm winds, the ''wave-blower'' who raises the waves and is appeased by Baltic-coast fishermen.'),
