 ('ENT_SLAV_PERUN','opposes','ENT_SLAV_VELES','high','The central reconstructed Slavic chaoskampf between the storm god Perun and the chthonic Veles.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_CHERNOBOG','opposes','ENT_SLAV_BELOBOG','low','The black/white-god dualism; Chernobog is attested in Helmold while Belobog is a reconstruction, so the opposition is scholarly.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_MARZANNA','opposes','ENT_SLAV_JARILO','medium','Marzanna (death/winter) and Jarilo (spring/fertility) form the reconstructed seasonal death-and-rebirth opposition.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_SVAROZHICH','child_of','ENT_SLAV_SVAROG','high','The name Svarozhich is a patronymic (''son of Svarog'').'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_DAZBOG','child_of','ENT_SLAV_SVAROG','high','The Hypatian interpolation in the Primary Chronicle names Dažbog as the son of Svarog.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_RADEGAST','aligned_with','ENT_SLAV_SVAROZHICH','medium','The Rethra deity is named Svarozhich by some chroniclers and Radegast by others; scholarship aligns the two.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_ROZHANITSY','aligned_with','ENT_SLAV_ROD','high','The Rozhanitsy are consistently invoked together with Rod as the birth-fate powers.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_SVETOVIT','presides_over','ENT_PROPHECY','high','Saxo describes the white-horse oracle of Svetovit at Arkona used to divine the future.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_SVETOVIT','presides_over','ENT_WAR','high','Svetovit is a war god whose horse, banner, and sword figure in martial divination per Saxo.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_RUGIEVIT','presides_over','ENT_WAR','high','Rugievit is a war god of the Rani per Saxo.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_YAROVIT','presides_over','ENT_WAR','high','Yarovit/Gerovit was equated with Mars by the Otto of Bamberg hagiographers.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_YAROVIT','presides_over','ENT_FERTILITY','medium','Yarovit is associated with spring fertility in the West-Slavic accounts.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_SVAROZHICH','presides_over','ENT_FIRE','high','Svarozhich personifies the sacred and hearth fire in the East-Slavic homiletic tradition.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_MARZANNA','presides_over','ENT_DEATH','medium','Marzanna/Morana personifies death and winter in Slavic seasonal custom.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_JARILO','presides_over','ENT_FERTILITY','medium','Jarilo is a spring/fertility figure of the seasonal folk cult.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_ZHIVA','presides_over','ENT_FERTILITY','medium','Zhiva''s name (''living'') connects her to life and fertility.'),
 ('ENT_SLAV_LADA','presides_over','ENT_LOVE','low','Lada is the putative (disputed) goddess of love and marriage.'),
